.TH BENCHMARK\-MEMORY\-PTS 1 "February 2026" "benchmarking" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh \- benchmark memory subsystem performance using the Phoronix Test Suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Benchmarks the memory subsystem using four complementary PTS test profiles that
together characterise sustained DRAM bandwidth, integer vs.\& floating-point memory
paths, cache hierarchy bandwidth, and combined bandwidth + latency across the full
L1/L2/L3/DRAM hierarchy.
All sub-option permutations (operation type, benchmark mode, access pattern) are
exercised automatically in a single run per test via PTS batch mode.
.PP
Before running tests the script checks the CPU frequency governor, thermal state,
system load, VM steal time, and Transparent Huge Pages state, and warns when
conditions may affect result validity.
.PP
PTS is installed automatically on supported distributions (Ubuntu, Debian,
Rocky Linux, openSUSE) if not already present.
.PP
Results are collected into
.B ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/
relative to the directory from which the script is invoked.
.SH PTS TESTS
.TP
.B pts/stream
Sustained DRAM bandwidth \(em Copy, Scale, Add, Triad operations.
.TP
.B pts/ramspeed
Integer and floating-point bandwidth \(em Copy, Scale, Add, Triad, Average.
.TP
.B pts/tinymembench
Bandwidth and access latency across L1/L2/L3 caches and DRAM.
.TP
.B pts/cachebench
Cache-level bandwidth \(em Read, Write, Read/Modify/Write.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upload
Upload results to OpenBenchmarking.org after the run completes.
Requires \fB\-\-result\-id\fR and \fB\-\-result\-name\fR.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-result\-id " " \fIID\fR
Short identifier for the run (e.g.\&
.IR dc1\-node3\-ddr5 ).
Used as the output directory name, the PTS result name prefix, and the upload
identifier on OpenBenchmarking.org.
Default: auto-generated timestamp string.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-result\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Human-readable display name for the result (e.g.\&
.IR "DC1 Node3 \- DDR5 6400 MT/s" ).
Required when \fB\-\-upload\fR is specified.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help message and exit.
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
.B ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/<result\-id>\-system\-snapshot.txt
System snapshot captured before the run: OS release, kernel version, CPU topology,
frequency scaling state, NUMA topology, THP state, DIMM information (dmidecode),
memory, and load average.
.TP
.BI ./benchmark\-results/<result\-id>/<result\-id>_ test /
One PTS result directory per test (e.g.\&
.BR <result\-id>_stream/ ,
.BR <result\-id>_ramspeed/ ,
\&...).
Each contains
.B composite.xml
and all result data for that test.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run all memory benchmarks:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run and upload results, labelled for later comparison:
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh \-\-upload \\
    \-\-result\-id "dc1\-node3\-ddr5" \\
    \-\-result\-name "DC1 Node3 \- DDR5 6400 MT/s"
.RE
.fi
.PP
Compare two runs with
.BR create\-report\-pts.sh (1):
.PP
.nf
.RS
\&./benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh \-\-result\-id "node3\-baseline"
\&./benchmark\-memory\-pts.sh \-\-result\-id "node3\-tuned"
\&./create\-report\-pts.sh \\
    ./benchmark\-results/node3\-baseline/ \\
    ./benchmark\-results/node3\-tuned/
.RE
.fi
